From db3900a74fc8465a223af697680ae27fc4cd3d92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dinakaran <dinakaranvijayakumar@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 06:17:39 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] loams-pg18: keep the fork's heap WAL format, without VM block
 references (D1112)

18.6 carries upstream's f581fa729d ("Fix VM clear WAL logging by
registering VM blocks"), the 18 back-patch of 17.11's c0d9864f. This
reverts its heapam.c and heapam_xlog.c changes and its pg_walsummary
t/002_blocks.pl change, and reverts 4d7feebfbd (pg_combinebackup
t/012_vm_consistency.pl), as the 17.11 merge did under option (a)
(docs/loams/pg17-vm-clear.md in ostrium-labs/loams-postgres; NF2 Task 1
F27). Kept from upstream: d0fb1da21b's block-reference macros,
visibilitymap_clear_locked() and pg_surgery's use of it.

The fork writes heap inserts, deletes, updates, multi-inserts and locks
as RM_NEON_ID records that carry the VM-cleared flags; the pageserver
derives the VM clear from them, and the decoder takes an update's old
heap block from the last block reference, which an extra VM block would
displace. The ported series' heap patch applies on top of this commit.

D1112 as amended on 2026-10-29: the owner ruled "Yes, revert at 18",
so option (a) extends to Postgres 18 and 18 matches 17 and 19.

Loams-Patch: LP-0037
Signed-off-by: Dinakaran <dinakaranvijayakumar@outlook.com>
